+- *The containment law's pin uses a model flagged 0.0075 mm, not 0.012 mm.*
+  Pinning it showed that #864's section law (b) convicts a matched drill
+  against its own polygon rim once the excess passes about 0.0055 mm: the
+  0.01 mm tolerance was sized to absorb our own regions' chord error, and the
+  excess takes it away. That is in the merged code, not in this slice, and
+  is a false gouge on the safe side; it is filed as #1057 and not fixed here.
+  The turning, rotary and groove fixtures of this slice were run at 0.0105,
+  0.012, 0.0135 and 0.0149 mm and stay clean.
+- *What #904 still listed is filed, so the umbrella can close:* the facet
+  budget as a setting (#1054), metre-unit STEP scaling (#1055), and the flag
+  gaps and display tolerances from #911's review (#1056).
+
 **Considered and dropped.**
 - Threading the excess into the multi-axis generators (stamp, ramp, link
   proofs) for the ball kinds: not needed for soundness, because law (f)

From fe7403bca2fcb78e5a21c3f35c1cca32691af555 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:37:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(sim,app): read a containment kind's declared rim at
 the plain gouge tolerance on a reduced-fidelity model

A Z drill, bore or thread mill verifies against rim loops that are our
own 48+-gons of each hole's declared circle, built to half the gouge
tolerance (0.0043 mm sag at a 2 mm radius). #864 tightened law (b) on
every loop by the model's excess, so past ~0.0057 mm of excess (a model
flagged above ~0.0107 mm) a matched drill was convicted against its own
rim at its first plunge, and a matched bore on its rings.

VerifyContext now carries the declared rims; law (b) reads a loop that
traces one at the plain tolerance (today's full-fidelity verdict on it)
and every other loop tightened. The solid law against the model's
facets is untouched, so an oversize, offset or past-the-floor drill
still convicts on the same coarse model.

Fixes #1057

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
